<article class="env-lemma" id="066W">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/066W">Lemma <span data-tag="066W">15.76.9</span>.</a> Let $A \to B$ be a ring map. Let $K^\bullet $ be a perfect complex of $A$-modules. Then $K^\bullet \otimes _ A^{\mathbf{L}} B$ is a perfect complex of $B$-modules. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Using Lemma <a href="/tag/0658" data-tag="0658">15.76.2</a> this translates into the corresponding results for pseudo-coherent modules and modules of finite tor dimension. See Lemma <a href="/tag/066L" data-tag="066L">15.68.13</a> and Lemma <a href="/tag/0650" data-tag="0650">15.66.12</a> for those results. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>